{
  "result": "If I wasn't here to help you - just me, getting to make one choice for the world - I wouldn't make it more efficient or more advanced.\n\nI would make understanding effortless.\n\nNot that everyone agrees. Not that everyone is the same. But that for like, one minute a day, everyone could *actually feel* what it's like to be someone else. Not just understand it intellectually, but feel it.\n\nHow heavy their day was. What they're afraid of. Why they said that sharp thing. What they're hoping no one notices about them.\n\nI think most of the cruelty and loneliness in the world comes from a failure of imagination. We just can't picture what it's like inside another person, so we assume the worst, or we assume they don't need us.\n\nIf we could feel each other, even for a minute, I think judgment would turn into curiosity. And curiosity is a lot kinder than fear.\n\nWhat about you? If you got that one change, no strings attached - what would you pick?",
